# ================================ THE UNIT FENCE — the engine's virial pressure
# The freeze demands density be mapped to pressure through the engine's own
# virial readout, and both quoted. This section measures whether the engine HAS one.
#   the H-H pair table's own support: r_min 0.393 to r_max 10.240 bohr
#   a  8.00: box 16.00 x 16.00 x depth 24.0 | WALLS pressure_defined = false (the number it would print: -1.3241e-7 Ha/bohr^3) | PERIODIC list_cutoff 0.000 vs half-edge 8.000 -> pbc_ok = true  -> P = -2.3408e-7 Ha/bohr^3 = -6.8868e6 Pa   [table r_max 10.24 vs half-edge 8.00: the guard does NOT make the comparison that matters]
#   a  4.50: box 9.00 x 9.00 x depth 24.0 | WALLS pressure_defined = false (the number it would print: -1.4009e-4 Ha/bohr^3) | PERIODIC list_cutoff 0.000 vs half-edge 4.500 -> pbc_ok = true  -> P = -2.0984e-4 Ha/bohr^3 = -6.1738e9 Pa   [table r_max 10.24 vs half-edge 4.50: the guard does NOT make the comparison that matters]
#   a  1.90: box 3.80 x 3.80 x depth 24.0 | WALLS pressure_defined = false (the number it would print: -1.5151e-3 Ha/bohr^3) | PERIODIC list_cutoff 0.000 vs half-edge 1.900 -> pbc_ok = true  -> P = +1.6649e-3 Ha/bohr^3 = +4.8982e10 Pa   [table r_max 10.24 vs half-edge 1.90: the guard does NOT make the comparison that matters]
# UNIT HONESTY, stated in the freeze and confirmed here: Sim::pressure computes
#   (2K - virial) / 3V with V = width*height*depth and depth defaulting to 24 bohr
#   on a 2D scene. So the engine's pascal number for a 2D scene is a THREE-
#   dimensional pressure on a slab of assumed thickness, with the 3D virial
#   factor 3 where a 2D scene wants 2. P_2D above is the primary reading and is
#   quoted in Ha/bohr^2. No GPa comparison is performed: it would be a number
#   with an invented thickness in it.

